OP_IRQ_SET arms an Irq with the bits it names, not those of them the capability it was bound with may signal,
so whoever holds the Irq signals bits its binder was never given;
an Irq is armed with no bit its notification capability may not signal.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: irq is armed with bits its notification capability may not signal

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -688,7 +688,6 @@ static int op_irq(const struct cap *cap, uint32_t op, uint32_t *arg)
         return KERR_STATE;
     }
     /* It signals on its binder's behalf, so only the bits the capability it was bound with may. */
-    bits &= irq->ntfn.b;
     if (bits == 0 && arg[1] != 0) {
         return KERR_NO_RIGHTS;
     }
